---
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';

const pubDate = new Date('2026-09-04');
---

<Layout
	title="My Research & The BMS Patient Survey"
	description="How I am using data tracking, pattern analysis, and AI to understand Burning Mouth Syndrome triggers and relief protocols."
	pubDate={pubDate}
>
	<div class="research-page">
		<p class="lead" style="font-size: 1.25rem; line-height: 1.75; color: var(--text-primary); margin-bottom: 2rem;">
			Burning Mouth Syndrome has remained a frustrating medical enigma largely because clinical research moves at a glacial pace. As a patient with a background in engineering and data, my goal is to build an open, structured dataset that uncovers real-world patterns across hundreds of sufferers.
		</p>
		
		<div style="background: #ffffff; border: 1px solid var(--card-border); padding: 3rem 2rem; border-radius: 24px; margin: 3rem 0; text-align: center; box-shadow: var(--shadow-md);">
			<span class="meta-tag" style="display: inline-block; margin-bottom: 1rem;">Patient-Led Science</span>
			<h3 style="color: var(--text-primary); margin-bottom: 0.75rem; font-size: 1.85rem; font-weight: 800;">The BMS Global Patient Survey</h3>
			<p style="color: var(--text-secondary); max-width: 560px; margin: 0 auto 2rem; font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.6;">
				I am currently preparing a comprehensive, multi-variable survey to systematically map out patient symptoms, anatomical locations, dietary triggers, and verified relief protocols.
			</p>
			
			<div style="max-width: 480px; margin: 0 auto;">
				<p style="font-weight: 700; color: var(--text-primary); margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">Want to contribute your experience?</p>
				<p style="font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">Join my waitlist to be notified the moment the survey launches and get full access to our findings.</p>
				
				<form action="/join" method="get" style="display: flex; gap: 0.75rem; max-width: 440px; margin: 0 auto;">
					<input 
						type="email" 
						name="email" 
						placeholder="Your email address..." 
						required 
						style="flex-grow: 1; padding: 0.85rem 1.25rem; border-radius: 100px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; background: #ffffff; color: var(--text-primary); font-size: 0.95rem; outline: none;" 
					/>
					<button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary" style="padding: 0.85rem 1.75rem; white-space: nowrap;">Notify Me</button>
				</form>
			</div>
		</div>

		<h2>Why I Am Applying AI to BMS Data</h2>
		<p>
			Traditional clinical trials often test single pharmaceutical molecules on small, homogeneous groups. But BMS symptoms are notoriously varied. AI and clustering algorithms are uniquely equipped to parse noisy, multi-dimensional patient data to identify distinct sub-types:
		</p>
		
		<ul style="line-height: 1.85; color: var(--text-secondary); margin-bottom: 2.5rem; font-size: 1.05rem;">
			<li><strong>Phenotype Clustering:</strong> Grouping patients who share similar onset triggers (e.g. dental trauma, viral illness, antibiotic use, menopause) to see which treatments work for their specific cluster.</li>
			<li><strong>Objective Protocol Scoring:</strong> Measuring which non-pharmacological interventions (nocturnal mouth taping, saliva stimulation, pH balancing) yield statistically significant relief.</li>
			<li><strong>Open Advocacy for Clinicians:</strong> Providing hard, structured metrics to ENTs, neurologists, and dental researchers so the medical establishment takes BMS seriously.</li>
		</ul>

		<p style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.6; font-style: italic;">
			Note: All data collected through this survey is completely anonymized, encrypted, and dedicated to benefiting the patient community.
		</p>
	</div>
</Layout>
